From af237b0f7561a64a311a2b5bd42c8f27d36d9867 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Roscoe <bryanroscoe@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:26:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 16/30] Parser: "~ is every nonbasic land type" (Planar Nexus)

Planar Nexus: "This land is every nonbasic land type. (Nonbasic land
types include Cave, Desert, Gate, Lair, Locus, Mine, Power-Plant, Sphere,
Tower, and Urza's.)"

CR 205.3i lists the land types; CR 305.6 names the five basic ones. The
line is a characteristic-defining ability (CR 604.3: printed on the land,
defines only its own subtypes, unconditional), so it functions in every
zone. phase parsed the sentence as an unimplemented spell effect, so the
land had no subtypes at all and Desert, Gate, Locus and Urza's payoffs
never counted it.

New ContinuousModification::AddAllNonbasicLandTypes (layer 4, additive,
no mana abilities: those come only with basic types), parsed from the
self-reference sentence as a CDA beside the "is every creature type"
form, and routed to the static parser by the classifier. Handled in every
exhaustive match, including phase-ai's (beneficial, like
AddAllLandTypes).

A sibling of AddAllBasicLandTypes and AddAllLandTypes rather than a
parameterized refactor of the three: the existing variants are in the
deployed card data, which must keep deserializing.

Tests: oracle_static tests self_ref_every_nonbasic_land_type_is_cda;
tests/integration/planar_nexus_every_nonbasic_land_type.rs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
